To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. Here's how the goal model can be structured:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|
| G1: Mission Completion | Complete the resource collection and delivery mission | - | Achieve | AND |
| G2: Resource Collection | Collect required resources from storage | FALLBACK(G3, G6) | Perform | OR |
| G3: Sequential Collection | Follow the order of storage based on waiting time and path | ; | Perform | AND |
| G4: Resource Request | Request resources from storage | - | Perform | AND |
| G5: Recharge or Reassign | Handle low battery during collection | FALLBACK(G7, G8) | Achieve | OR |
| G6: Parallel Collection | Assign multiple robots for parallel collection | # | Perform | OR |
| G7: Recharge | Recharge robot at station | - | Achieve | AND |
| G8: Reassign Mission | Reassign mission to another robot | - | Achieve | AND |
| G9: Resource Delivery | Deliver resources to specified location | FALLBACK(G10, G11) | Perform | OR |
| G10: Sequential Delivery | Deliver all resources to destination | ; | Perform | AND |
| G11: Low Battery Handling | Handle low battery during delivery | FALLBACK(G12, G13) | Achieve | OR |
| G12: Return to Checkpoint | Return resource to checkpoint | - | Achieve | AND |
| G13: Trigger Alert | Trigger alert for failure to return | - | Perform | AND |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|
| AT1: Navigate to Storage | Navigate to the specified storage location | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT2: Send Resource Request | Send message to storage for resource request | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT3: Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are retrieved | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT4: Navigate to Recharging Station | Navigate to recharging station | AND | Recharging Station | 1 |
| AT5: Reassign Collection Task | Reassign collection task to another robot | AND | - | 1 |
| AT6: Navigate to Delivery Location | Navigate to delivery location | AND | Delivery Location | 1 |
| AT7: Deliver Resources | Deliver resources to destination | AND | Delivery Location | 1 |
| AT8: Return to Checkpoint | Return resource to checkpoint | AND | Checkpoint | 1 |
| AT9: Trigger Alert | Trigger alert for failure | AND | - | 1 |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G9 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G3, G4, G5 [AND]**
- **G3 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**
- **G4 -> AT4 [AND]**
- **G5 -> G7, G8 [OR]**
- **G6 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [PARALLEL]**
- **G7 -> AT4 [AND]**
- **G8 -> AT5 [AND]**
- **G9 -> G10, G11 [AND]**
- **G10 -> AT6, AT7 [SEQUENTIAL]**
- **G11 -> G12, G13 [OR]**
- **G12 -> AT8 [AND]**
- **G13 -> AT9 [AND]**

This model ensures that the mission is broken down into manageable tasks and goals, with clear dependencies and execution strategies for both collection and delivery phases.
